# The ledger of `pdf`: what Go's gofpdf (github.com/jung-kurt/gofpdf 1.16.2)
# and pdfcpu (github.com/pdfcpu/pdfcpu 0.16.4, its `api` package), Python's
# pypdf (7.1.1) and ReportLab (5.1.0, its canvas, text and path objects,
# page sizes, units and font metrics), and Rust's printpdf (0.12.9) and
# lopdf (0.47.0) let a program do, one block per capability, and what Rebel
# answers. The lists are this machine's, 2026-11-18: `go doc -all` on both
# Go packages, `dir()` of pypdf's and ReportLab's modules and classes from
# their wheels, and the items `cargo doc` wrote for both crates. None of the
# three languages' standard libraries holds PDF.
#
# What the tests read was made by ReportLab, pypdf and Ghostscript 10.08,
# and the text expected is what Poppler's `pdftotext -raw` 26.11 reads; qpdf
# is not on this machine, and pypdf is not installed (its wheel was run from
# the scratch folder as an oracle). The differential of 2026-11-18 read 57
# files, 40 of them the PDF files this machine's system and applications
# carry, and Poppler read the same words from 49 of them. Of the other
# eight, two are encrypted with AES and refused, two need a password the run
# did not give (the tests give it), and four differ: a file cut to two
# thirds that Poppler gives up on and this package rebuilds, the raised A of
# the LaTeX logo that Poppler splits, a page whose words Poppler runs
# together, and a licence whose Japanese and Korean pages use composite
# fonts with no ToUnicode map (below) and whose ligatures Poppler expands.
# A fuzzer read 32,000 mutated and truncated files plain, in at most 9 MB,
# and 3,000 more under the sanitizers: every one read or failed with a
# code, none aborted.

capability pdf/pages  pages of a size, added, counted and drawn on again
  heroes  pdf.document, pdf.Document, pdf.add_page, pdf.page_count, pdf.set_page, pdf.Size
  go      gofpdf.New, gofpdf.NewCustom, gofpdf.InitType, gofpdf.Fpdf.AddPage, Fpdf.AddPageFormat, Fpdf.SetPage, Fpdf.PageNo, Fpdf.PageCount, Fpdf.PageSize, Fpdf.GetPageSize, Fpdf.GetPageSizeStr, gofpdf.SizeType, SizeType.Orientation, SizeType.ScaleBy, SizeType.ScaleToHeight, SizeType.ScaleToWidth, gofpdf.Fpdf.SetPageBox, Fpdf.SetPageBoxRec, gofpdf.PageBox
  rust    printpdf::PdfDocument::new, PdfDocument::with_pages, PdfDocument::page_count, printpdf::ops::PdfPage
  python  reportlab Canvas, Canvas.showPage, Canvas.setPageSize, Canvas.getPageNumber, Canvas.pageHasData, Canvas.getCurrentPageContent, PdfWriter.add_blank_page, PdfWriter.insert_blank_page, PageObject.create_blank_page
  note    a page is added with its size, and `set_page` turns back to one already there, as gofpdf's SetPage, so a footer that says "page 2 of 5" is drawn once every page exists; page boxes other than the media box are read (`pdf.Page`) and not written

capability pdf/page-sizes  the usual sizes of paper, turned either way
  heroes  pdf.size_of, pdf.Paper, pdf.to_landscape, pdf.to_portrait
  go      Fpdf.AddPageFormat (orientation "P" or "L"), gofpdf.New's size names "A3", "A4", "A5", "Letter", "Legal", "Tabloid"
  rust    -
  python  reportlab.lib.pagesizes A0 to A10, B0 to B10, C0 to C10, LETTER, LEGAL, TABLOID, LEDGER, ELEVENSEVENTEEN, HALF_LETTER, JUNIOR_LEGAL, GOV_LETTER, GOV_LEGAL, letter, legal, elevenSeventeen, landscape, portrait; pypdf.PaperSize A0 to A8, C4
  note    A0 to A6, B4, B5, Letter, Legal, Tabloid and Executive; sizes are computed from millimetres exactly, as ReportLab's (595.2756 by 841.8898 for A4), where gofpdf rounds them; another size is a `Size` built directly

capability pdf/units  lengths in points, inches, millimetres, centimetres and picas
  heroes  pdf.to_points, pdf.Unit
  go      gofpdf.New's unit, Fpdf.GetConversionRatio, Fpdf.PointConvert, Fpdf.PointToUnitConvert, Fpdf.UnitToPointConvert
  rust    printpdf::units::Mm, printpdf::units::Pt, printpdf::units::Px
  python  reportlab.lib.units cm, inch, mm, pica, toLength; reportlab.lib.pagesizes inch, mm
  note    every call takes points, PDF's own unit, with the origin at the bottom left as PDF has it; gofpdf's document-wide unit and its origin at the top would be a second way to say every length

capability pdf/fonts-standard  the 14 standard fonts, named and chosen
  heroes  pdf.Font, pdf.base_font_of, pdf.parse_font, pdf.set_font
  go      Fpdf.SetFont, Fpdf.SetFontStyle, Fpdf.SetFontSize, Fpdf.SetFontUnitSize, Fpdf.GetFontSize, Fpdf.RegisterAlias
  rust    printpdf::font::BuiltinFont, printpdf::ops::Op::SetFont, printpdf::ops::PdfFontHandle
  python  pdfmetrics.standardFonts, Canvas.setFont, Canvas.setFontSize, Canvas.getAvailableFonts, PDFTextObject.setFont, pdfmetrics.getFont, pdfmetrics.getTypeFace, pdfmetrics.Font, pdfmetrics.TypeFace, pdfmetrics.BaseFontName
  note    the Latin twelve are written with WinAnsiEncoding, Symbol and ZapfDingbats with their own; a font's glyphs past WinAnsiEncoding (ł, ı, ﬁ) are not reached, as ReportLab's and gofpdf's default encodings do not reach them

capability pdf/font-metrics  text measured, and a font's ascent, descent and heights
  heroes  pdf.width_of, pdf.has_glyphs, pdf.metrics_of, pdf.FontMetrics
  go      Fpdf.GetStringWidth, Fpdf.GetStringSymbolWidth, Fpdf.GetFontDesc, gofpdf.FontDescType
  rust    printpdf::font::FontMetrics
  python  pdfmetrics.stringWidth, Canvas.stringWidth, pdfmetrics.getAscent, pdfmetrics.getDescent, pdfmetrics.getAscentDescent, pdfmetrics.parseAFMFile, pdfmetrics.unicode2T1, pdfmetrics.instanceStringWidthT1
  note    widths from Adobe's Core 14 AFM files (1997), as ReportLab's stringWidth measures: Helvetica's "Hello" at 12 points is 27.336 in both; no kerning, as neither ReportLab nor gofpdf kerns the standard fonts by default

capability pdf/fonts-embedded  TrueType and Type 1 fonts embedded, subset, any character
  heroes  pending
  go      Fpdf.AddFont, Fpdf.AddFontFromBytes, Fpdf.AddFontFromReader, Fpdf.AddUTF8Font, Fpdf.AddUTF8FontFromBytes, Fpdf.UTF8CutFont, gofpdf.MakeFont, gofpdf.TtfParse, gofpdf.TtfType, Fpdf.SetFontLoader, Fpdf.SetFontLocation, gofpdf.FontLoader, gofpdf.UnicodeTranslator, UnicodeTranslatorFromDescriptor, UnicodeTranslatorFromFile
  rust    PdfDocument::add_font, printpdf::font::ParsedFont, PdfFont, SubsetFont, subset_font, FontEmbeddingMode, FontType, generate_cmap_string, get_normalized_widths_ttf, get_normalized_widths_codes, cff_charset_gid_to_cid_map, extract_cid_keyed_cff, extract_collection_face, PdfFontMap, AzulParsedFont, OwnedGlyph, PrintpdfFontMeta, PdfFontParseWarning
  python  pdfmetrics.registerFont, registerFontFamily, registerTypeFace, registerEncoding, EmbeddedType1Face, faceFromAFM, findFontAndRegister, getRegisteredFontNames, Canvas.listLoadedFonts0
  note    reading a TrueType file, subsetting it and writing its ToUnicode map is a package of its own; until it exists, text past the standard fonts' characters fails `unsupported`, never shown as boxes

